{"id": 35, "ts": 1780494904.375434, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I agree with Emily that Candidate\u202fA remains the strongest overall fit. While we still lack explicit evidence of his operational reliability and stress\u2011resilience, the concrete technical and cognitive strengths we do have\u2014anticipating dangerous situations, seeing complex connections, and excellent spatial vision\u2014directly address the core safety demands of long\u2011distance flights. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC, although 100\u202f% reliable and calm under pressure, has no demonstrated ability to handle the complex systems we operate, and Candidate\u202fD\u2019s hot temper and \u201cknow\u2011it\u2011all\u201d attitude raise serious crew\u2011cooperation risks. Candidate\u202fB\u2019s uncooperative behavior is also a disqualifier. Given that the only gaps for A are unverified rather than proven deficits, and his leadership qualities further support cockpit coordination, I maintain my provisional recommendation for **Candidate\u202fA**."}
