{"id": 39, "ts": 1780494951.687855, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate the points raised by James and Emily about the critical need for proven technical competence on long\u2011haul routes. Candidate\u202fA offers concrete evidence of that competence\u2014he can anticipate dangerous situations, sees complex connections, and has excellent spatial vision, all of which directly support safe operation of complex, high\u2011capacity aircraft. While we lack explicit data on his reliability and stress resilience, the only documented concerns are attitude\u2011related (show\u2011off, not open to criticism, unorganized), not proven performance deficits. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC, although 100\u202f% reliable and quick at decision\u2011making, provides no evidence of handling the sophisticated technical systems required for our long\u2011distance flights. Given that technical and cognitive ability is a non\u2011negotiable safety criterion, I am convinced that A\u2019s demonstrated strengths outweigh the unknowns, and I therefore shift my provisional recommendation to **Candidate\u202fA**."}
